  <div class="center"> <img src="../images/ephemera/50bro026.jpg" alt="Bolex Vacation Movies" width="262" height="484"> 
    <div class="imagecap">3 2/8" x 6", double-sided, six panel fold-out (12 panels). 
      New York: Paillard Products, Inc. (195?). </div>
  </div>
  <p>I don't really know the story behind this pamphlet. I can only assume it 
    was available at Bolex franchised dealers in the US, or mailed to customers. 
    My copy is stamped on the rear for: Main Camera Center Inc., 332 Main St. 
    East, Rochester 4, N.Y. </p>
  <p>It contains general tips for shooting vacation movies; in particular, considerations 
    for shooting beach and water scenes (exposure and care of the equipment). 
    It also includes a check list of equipment you may want to take with you on 
    your trip. On the other side is a collage of scenic photographs; most appear 
    to have been taken from issues of the Bolex Reporter. </p>
